WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:13.080
Hi! Let's set up the Trikey Guardian on your Umbrel. It holds key three of your wallet, on a server you own.

2
00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:25.550
Before you start, you need an Umbrel with Bitcoin Node and Electrs, both on the network you'll test on. Signet is the easiest. And let Electrs finish syncing first.

3
00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:36.135
In the App Store, open the menu, choose Community App Stores, and add the Trikey store. Paste the address rather than typing it.

4
00:00:52.086 --> 00:01:00.274
Open the Trikey store and install Trikey Guardian. Umbrel adds Bitcoin Node and Electrs too, if they're missing.

5
00:01:13.070 --> 00:01:19.550
Then open it from your Umbrel's home screen. Always use the icon: it goes through Umbrel's login.

6
00:01:20.570 --> 00:01:28.634
One thing to get right: your passphrase. There's no way to reset it, so write it down and keep it somewhere safe.

7
00:01:29.220 --> 00:01:40.324
Choose a passphrase and type it twice. The green check means the guardian found your node and Electrs. Leave the relays as they are, unless you know you need others.

8
00:01:45.310 --> 00:01:50.913
Your guardian is ready. It shows a pairing code, which you'll scan with the app when you create your wallet.

9
00:01:54.810 --> 00:02:05.837
After a restart, the guardian locks itself, so a stolen box is useless. Unlock it from the Trikey app with your hardware wallet, or type your passphrase here.

10
00:02:09.630 --> 00:02:18.686
That's it, your guardian is ready. Next, let's install the Trikey app on your phone.
